  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material as the subject of the motivational claim",
  "description": "The user is implicitly projected onto the text 'this project is tough but it will save the world', which frames the user as the one undertaking the 'tough project'. The user is not explicitly addressed with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but the motivational text creates an implicit identification with the speaker or doer of the project, making the user the projected subject of the statement. The user is projected onto the textual material to identify with the 'project' being described.",
